@startuml gapanalysis-module-internal
' Ports-and-adapters inside the Gap Analysis module, as implemented at the end of Step 5.
' Dependencies point inwards only; the domain ring knows no framework.
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "competency.api (named interface)" {
  [CompetencyId · CompetencyFrameworkId] as CID
  [CompetencyModelSnapshot] as SNAP
  [CompetencyModelRegistered\n(integration event)] as EVT
}

package "learner.api (named interface)" {
  [LearnerId] as LID
  [LearnerAttainmentQuery\nAttainedCompetency] as LAQ
  [LearnerIdentityQuery] as LIQ
}

package "gapanalysis.api (named interface)" {
  [SkillGapId] as SGID
}

package "domain.model — authored" {
  [GapReport\n(aggregate root)] as REPORT
  [SkillGap\n(one finding)] as GAP
  [AnalysisTarget\n(what it was measured against)] as TGT
  [AttainmentSnapshot\n(what was attained, or absent)] as ATT
  [EvidenceSnapshot\n(provenance, owned here)] as EVS
  [GapSeverity · GapReportId] as GVO
  [GapReportSummary\n(read model)] as SUM
  [NotFound · ForbiddenScope ·\nNotProjected · UnknownTargetLevel] as EXC
}

package "domain.model — derived (ADR-007)" {
  [ProjectedCompetencyModel] as PMODEL
  [ProjectedCompetency · ProjectedLevel] as PCOMP
}

package "domain.policy" {
  [GapSeverityPolicy\n(domain service port)] as POL
  [OrdinalDistanceSeverityPolicy\n(default)] as ODP
}

package "domain (driven ports)" {
  [GapReportRepository] as RREPO
  [CompetencyModelProjectionRepository] as PREPO
}

package "application" {
  [GapAnalysisService\n(transaction boundary · ownership)] as SVC
  [AnalyseGapCommand] as CMD
  [GapAnalysisModuleConfiguration] as MCFG
}

package "infrastructure.web" {
  [GapReportController\n/api/gap-reports] as CTRL
  [GapAnalysisWebMapper] as WMAP
  [ExceptionHandler -> RFC 9457] as EXH
  [Request / Response DTOs] as DTO
}

package "infrastructure.projection" {
  [CompetencyModelProjectionListener\n@ApplicationModuleListener] as LIS
}

package "infrastructure.persistence" {
  [JpaGapReportRepository] as JRR
  [JpaCompetencyModelProjectionRepository] as JPR
  [GapReport · SkillGap · GapEvidence\nJPA entities (V401)] as ENT1
  [ProjectedFramework · ProjectedCompetency\nJPA entities (V400)] as ENT2
}

CTRL --> SVC
CTRL --> WMAP
CTRL --> DTO
CTRL --> EXH
WMAP --> CMD
SVC --> CMD
SVC --> REPORT
SVC --> RREPO
SVC --> PREPO
SVC --> POL
SVC --> EXC
SVC --> LAQ
SVC --> LIQ
MCFG --> ODP

REPORT --> GAP
REPORT --> LID
REPORT --> GVO
GAP --> SGID
GAP --> TGT
GAP --> ATT
GAP --> POL
TGT --> CID
ATT --> EVS
PMODEL --> PCOMP
PCOMP --> CID
ODP .up.|> POL

LIS --> EVT
LIS --> SNAP
LIS --> PREPO
JRR .up.|> RREPO
JRR --> ENT1
JPR .up.|> PREPO
JPR --> ENT2
JPR --> PMODEL
RREPO --> SUM

note right of REPORT
  ADR-021: a report is SELF-CONTAINED and stated as of an
  instant. Every finding carries its own target, attainment
  and provenance, so Recommendation can synthesise a pathway
  without reaching back into the contexts that produced them
  — which is what keeps the module DAG acyclic.

  Invariant inside the boundary: at most one finding per
  competency, enforced in generate() AND reconstitute(), and
  backed at rest by uq_skill_gap_report_competency.

  No mutators and no invalidation. Recomputation adds a
  report; it never replaces one, so history survives.
end note

note bottom of ATT
  ABSENCE IS MODELLED BY ABSENCE. A competency nothing has
  been measured for holds no snapshot at all — not a
  zero-ordinal one — and the distinction survives storage
  (three nullable columns under ck_skill_gap_attainment_complete)
  and serialisation (the field is omitted, not zeroed).

  "Never assessed" and "assessed at the lowest level" are
  different problems calling for different remedies: an
  assessment, not a learning intervention.
end note

note bottom of EVS
  Gap Analysis OWNS this type rather than reusing Learner
  Profiling's published EvidenceSummary. A stored report must
  stay explicable indefinitely, and reusing another context's
  contract would make every historical report's shape hostage
  to that contract's evolution. The copy is taken in
  GapAnalysisService, at the boundary — the anti-corruption
  step ADR-021's snapshot rule requires.
end note

note right of POL
  ADR-021: severity is the one genuine judgement here, so it
  is the only thing whose variation is interesting. Two
  methods, not one taking a nullable attainment — absence is
  a different question ("what does it mean that nothing was
  measured") and splitting it stops a policy sliding into
  treating unassessed as a shortfall from zero.

  Third independent use of the substitutable-strategy
  technique, after ADR-006 and ADR-018, which is what makes
  it an architectural property rather than a one-off.
end note

note bottom of PMODEL
  ADR-007 / ADR-022: the one CQRS surface in the system.
  DERIVED — nothing here is authored, the source of truth
  stays in competency.framework_model, and a defect is
  repaired by replaying the event rather than migrating data.

  Held as flat rows so gap computation never traverses an
  EMF graph; compilation happens inside Competency Modelling
  before publication, because ADR-012 forbids an EObject from
  crossing the boundary at all.
end note

note bottom of LIS
  Event delivery is a delivery mechanism, exactly as HTTP is,
  so the listener sits in the adapter ring.
  @ApplicationModuleListener makes it asynchronous AND
  transactional: async so a projection failure cannot roll
  back the registration that triggered it, transactional so
  the durable registry marks delivery complete only when the
  consuming transaction commits.

  Redelivery is therefore expected and harmless — the write
  is a replacement, not an append.
end note

note bottom of CTRL
  Ownership authorisation (ADR-015 Amendment 2) is enforced
  in two places, and neither is sufficient alone:

  (1) SecurityConfig (platform) — one ordered chain rule
        /api/gap-reports/** -> authenticated()
      No role rule, and its ABSENCE is the decision: every
      operation is learner-scoped, which is precisely what a
      URL pattern cannot express.
  (2) GapAnalysisService — the caller's subject resolved to a
        LearnerId via learner.api, then compared.

  TWO DENIAL SHAPES, because the disclosure differs:
    GET /{id}            -> 404 for absent AND forbidden; a
                            lookup happened, so 403 would
                            confirm the report exists — and a
                            report names its learner.
    POST · GET ?learnerId -> 403; the identifier came from the
                            caller and is never looked up, so
                            refusing discloses nothing.
end note

note right of SVC
  ADR-016: the caller's subject arrives as a command field,
  never from SecurityContextHolder — a rule
  applicationStaysOutOfAdapters enforces. The whole ownership
  matrix is therefore exercisable with no security context,
  no token and no Spring container, which
  GapAnalysisServiceTests demonstrates rather than asserts.

  callerMayAnalyseAnyLearner is a DECISION, not a role: the
  security layer resolves the role question and passes a
  boolean, so this module never meets the Role type, which
  lives in platform and which its DAG forbids it to reach.
end note

note bottom of JRR
  ADR-020's test applied a second time: relational, not jsonb,
  because a report's shape is fixed by Java types and two of
  its invariants are expressible only as constraints.

  Rehydration goes exclusively through reconstitute(). Running
  a GapSeverityPolicy on load would silently restate a
  historical judgement under whatever rule is configured
  today, and would mint fresh ids for findings that already
  have published ones.
end note
@enduml
